## Complete-run remediation — 2026-11-13

Maintainer selected all cargo-deny findings. Preserve GPL-3.0-only and Iced 0.14. Review cached package license files and exact declaration/resolved edges; unify only compatible ranges in an isolated/offline lock candidate. Explicitly allow BSL-1.0 after comparison with Boost text/GNU compatibility classification. Exact older-version dispositions retain deny-by-default for unknown generations; no skip-tree. Current report records native checks and distribution limitations. Supporting application-security entry .codex/skills/application-security/SKILL.md (bridge sdd/chain/application-security.md version 1) was actually consulted for dependency control and evidence; primary software-delivery and Rust contributions are recorded in scripts-centralization's remediation plan.

## R3 verification dependency repair — 2026-11-18

Scope: the real OSV finding for lru 0.16.4 discovered during the authorized R3
verification. The user separately authorized downloading exactly lru 0.18.5; its
archive checksum was verified. This does not authorize other acquisition or central
Toolbox maintenance. Keep Iced/wgpu/cosmic-text and the configured renderer unchanged.

D-05/R-05: use the cached published cryoglyph source with a bounded path patch,
retaining upstream source/examples/benches/samples/licenses. The initial dependency-
only proposal produced two actual Opengrep findings; replace those two raw casts
with derived Pod proofs and safe byte views, preserving field order, sizes and
zero-copy behavior. No new rule, baseline, advisory or source exclusion is added.
The vendor remains outside automatic workspace membership; its actual unit tests
have a separate maintained entry. The workspace lock remains operative and scanned.

Decision: docs/decisions/locked-lru-remediation.md. Owner: R3 coordinator for the
